  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 320,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, so have sports become a big dumb investment \nbubble? It might sound like a silly question  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6160,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because well, everything has become a big dumb \ninvestment bubble, but sports in particular are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11120,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "going through something of a truly unprecedented \nvalue boom. And perhaps the only reason we aren't  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15760,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "really noticing it is because none of us are \nin the market for a professional sports team.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20320,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Last month, a truly nightmare rotation of Bob \nIger and Jared Kushner's little brother's Thrive  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24960,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Capital agreed to purchase the LA Lakers for a \nrecord-breaking 122.5 billion just a year after it  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31200,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was sold the last time for a previously record- \nsetting $10 billion. Across the wider market  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36400,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for these teams, the NBA index, if you will, has \nreturned 2,88% returns over the same period that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43200,
    "dDurationMs": 7680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even a record bull run from the S\u0026P 500 returned \na measly 687%. But there is one problem with this.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50880,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sports teams are terrible businesses. They are \ncapital inensive with massive overhead, run on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56960,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "razor thin margins, are subject to arbitrary rule \nchanges by governing bodies directly exposed to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62320,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wider market volatility. They are illquid. And \nthere is also the additional variable that if  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67040,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your team doesn't actually win, it can slowly \nbleed value even if the rest of the business is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72000,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "run flawlessly. Now, back in the day, none of this \nreally mattered. Even prestigious sporting leagues  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77600,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ran on pretty shoestream budgets. The players \nmade decent money, but nothing that far out of the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82800,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ordinary, and the whole thing was held together \nby fan support, a sprinkling of sponsor dollars,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87600,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a dream. Of course, over the last three \ndecades, that has made way for billionaires  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92400,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spending hundreds of millions of dollars to play \nFantasy League with better graphics. The regular  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96720,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "operations made some money, lost some money, but \noverall, they were largely a vanity asset rather  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101680,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than something that was a purely financial play. \nBut today, even that is changing. A lot of sports  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107120,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "teams are getting too valuable for even regular \nrun-of-the-mill billionaires. They have become  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111760,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "institutionalized assets that are the investing \ndomain of private equity, public companies,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116160,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and even sovereign wealth funds. Infamously, \none of the key signals of investing mania is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121120,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an uptick in fraud surrounding an asset. \nAnd we will get to that. In the meantime,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125600,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this has clearly been bad for sports fans. But \nif this really is such a terrible business,  "
    } ]
